senses.gloss:
vaineya (in mg. 1 = Pali veneyya; cf. vineya),
(1) adj. or subst. m. = vineya 1, one that is to be (religiously) trained, or converted: ˚yā(ḥ) LV 〔437.11〕; ˚ya-sattvānāṃ Mv 〔i.314.2〕; buddha-vai˚, to be converted by the B., Mv 〔i.314.3〕; Divy 〔150.20〕; Av 〔i.67.6〕; ˚ya-prābhṛta Divy 〔36.21〕 a gift of a prospective convert, see prābhṛta; na tu ˚yavatsānāṃ Buddho velām atikramet Divy 〔96.6〕 = Av 〔i.17.6〕; ˚ya-jana Divy 〔96.9〕; ˚yāpekṣayā 〔49.8〕; 〔330.7〕; darśana-˚yānāṃ sattvānāṃ śravaṇa-˚yānāṃ etc. Gv 〔348.24 ff.〕; others, Divy 〔202.29〕 etc.; Av 〔ii.176.3 f.〕; Kv 〔21.22 ff.〕;
(2) subst. (nt.? not recorded in Pali; cf. vineya 2), religious training, esp. conversion: vaineya-vaśena, ˚vaśam upādāya, see s.v. vaśa; sattva-vaineya-kāraṇāt SP 〔228.8〕, for the sake of conversion of creatures; tasya ca vaineya-kālaṃ jñātvā Divy 〔330.10〕, knowing it was time for his conversion.
